## Findings — store 99 (all fixed)

**1. Restroom block interior was walkable floor** — `(601.7, 675.7)–(670.7, 719.7)`
Crop `walkable_overlay` 3×3 cell (2,1), confirmed by a 300-dpi mask render of pt 480–700 × 650–740 and a 2-pt line scan: rows y=688…718 are reachable at x 602-606, 630-634, 638-640, 664-668 — the open floor on both sides of the T-partition stem, i.e. both toilet-room interiors plus the vestibule. Bay is walled at x=601.7/670.7, entered through one 29-pt mouth at (620.8–650.1, y=674), split by the drawn T (bar y=683.7–685.9, stem x=636.2–638.4). No fixture, no product label, no frontage inside. Truth: enclosed room, not sales floor (cf. 24 `Restrooms interior`, 660 `restroom vestibule…(enclosed room)`, 658 restroom block exclusion). **Fix: exclusion rect** `[601,675,671,721]`. The `RESTROOMS` anchor at (637.3,665.4) is north of the mouth and still snaps to alley floor.

**2. Tobacco kiosk back room was walkable** — `(551, 676)–(598, 720)`, 19 m²
Same mask render; the line scan shows its **only** link to the alley is a 4-pt slit at x=594–598, y=674 between the counter's east end and the restroom wall — 0.4 m, not a customer corridor. The bay is walled west (x=551) and roofed by the counter wall x=551–588, with the sawtooth-faced Tobacco fixture `[551.4,667,593.4,676]` standing on it facing **north** into the alley. Empty walled floor behind a service counter = staff (cf. 265/269/811). Also confirmed by the "green floor >2.6 m from any printed text" scan, which listed it as a 10.8 m² textless cluster at centroid (574,706). **Fix: exclusion rect** `[550,674,600,721]`.

